"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nI visited this place after traveling on the Haeundae Beach Train.  \nIt wasn't a place I visited with high expectations, but the view was much better than I thought.  \n\nAt the entrance, there was a decoration showing the cafe's identity.  \nCompared to the atmosphere at the entrance, the interior felt surprisingly clean and modern.  \n\nSeeing a note that they serve it with an egg yolk, I ordered ssanghwa-tang (traditional herbal tea) and an iced americano without hesitation.  \n\nThe ssanghwa-tang was on the sweeter side and was packed with nuts.  \nPersonally, I thought it could have been a bit less sweet.  \n\nOn the contrary, the coffee suited my taste better as it was savory with low acidity.  \n\nI spent a relaxing time sitting in a spot perfect for spacing out while looking at the sea.\n## Pictures\n\n\n\n\n\n\n"